  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 028b1116645bd8b4981650adf501c6d8, type: 3}
  m_Name: Campaign
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Game.Stage::Game.Stage.Config.CampaignAsset
  _title: The Last Architects
  _prologue: 'The old wards have failed. From the broken lands beyond the rim, hordes
    march on the last free valleys, and no army of steel can stop them.


    Only
    the mages can. Their towers bind fire, water, ice and storm into weapons that
    feed on one another: water carries lightning, frost makes stone shatter, oil
    begs for a spark.


    But towers do not raise themselves. You are the Chief
    Architect of the Circle of Mages. You choose where every tower stands and how
    the elements meet. Place them well, and the realm endures. Place them poorly,
    and there will be nothing left to defend.'
  _defeat: 'The enemy broke through. Regroup, rethink the layout and try again: the
    realm cannot afford a second fall.'
